# Copy to .env.local for local development.

# Signs the session cookie. Required in production; a development fallback is
# used when it is unset, and the app refuses to start a production build
# without it. Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# DEMO AUTH ONLY — not a production identity service.
# Seed accounts for the prototype, as:
#   username|password|Display Name|Job title|ACCESS_ROLE
# ACCESS_ROLE is optional and is AUTHORIZED_USER unless it says ADMINISTRATOR.
# At least one ADMINISTRATOR is needed or nobody can review a dataset request;
# /api/auth/status reports it when there is none.
# People who register on the platform itself get AUTHORIZED_USER and do not
# belong here — this is only how a deployment seeds its first administrator.
# Separate multiple accounts with a semicolon. When unset, development falls
# back to demo@chigari.org / chigari-demo and logs a warning.
# The quotes below are for this file's sake. A hosting dashboard wants the
# value on its own, though a wrapping pair is stripped if it comes along.
DEMO_AUTH_USERS="demo@chigari.org|chigari-demo|Demo Officer|Field officer|ADMINISTRATOR"
